## Why This Is Asked

Real-world webhook reliability and security require resilience to duplicate deliveries, key rotation, and downstream retries under load. This tests knowledge of idempotent processing, signature validation, and observability across services.

## Key Concepts

- Webhook reliability and exactly-once semantics
- HMAC verification with rotating keys
- Deduplication using eventId and race-condition handling
- Replay protection and retry/backoff strategies
- Observability, metrics, and tracing for webhook pipelines

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: verify signature and idempotency
function handleWebhook(req) {
  const key = getCurrentSigningKey();
  const valid = verifyHmac(req.body, req.headers['X-Signature'], key);
  if (!valid) return 401;
  if (isEventProcessed(req.body.eventId)) return 200;
  processEvent(req.body); // write upsert, emit downstream task
  return 200;
}
```

